# The raw record of one measurement run -- the host, its load, the per-round samples -- is not
# tracked. It is one run's file, it changes with the host and its load, and a clone would carry
# readings taken once somewhere else. The numbers the pages quote are in their tables; the files
# stay with the run, on the machine that took it, under the names the pages cite.
results/
results.json
accuracy.json
artifacts/
__pycache__/